    {
      "filename": "Moeraki Boulders (13) (8137768453).jpg",
      "title": "File:Moeraki Boulders (13) (8137768453).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Moeraki_Boulders_%2813%29_%288137768453%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moeraki_Boulders_(13)_(8137768453).jpg",
      "width": 2400,
      "height": 1556,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC0",
      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en",
      "artist": "Bernard Spragg. NZ from Christchurch, New Zealand",
      "description": "he Moeraki Boulders are unusually large and spherical boulders lying along a stretch of Koekohe Beach on the wave cut Otago coast of New Zealand between Moeraki and Hampden. They occur scattered either as isolated or clusters of boulders within a stretch of beach where they have been protected in a scientific reserve. The erosion by wave action of mudstone, comprising local bedrock and landslides, frequently exposes embedded isolated boulders. These boulders are grey-colored septarian concretions, which have been exhumed from the mudstone enclosing them and concentrated on the beach by coastal erosion",
      "dateCreated": "2010-07-10 11:31",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "moeraki-boulders-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "pzcq",
      "mediumPath": "_m/p/z/c/q/moeraki-boulders-wp/moeraki-boulders-13-8137768453-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/p/z/c/q/moeraki-boulders-wp/moeraki-boulders-13-8137768453-small.webp"
    },
    {
